\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Falls To New Low Despite RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1996\par 12:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-DJ)--The Indian rupee fell to a new all-time low against the dollar Friday, despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the slide. \par \par \uc2  Traders said heavy dollar demand from companies continued to outweigh sporadic dollar sales by the Reserve Bank of India, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a new high around 36.80 rupees in afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2  They added that the outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains bleak, despite continuing comments from Indian officials that present dollar levels aren't justified by the current economic situation. \par \par \uc2  'The pressure is unabated,' a trader at a foreign bank in Bombay said, noting that companies remain panicked by the recent rupee slide and are continuing to load up on dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers widely agreed that the heavy dollar demand has been prompted by the Reserve Bank's failure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or make any other significant rupee-supportive move. They predicted the dollar will rise above 37.00 rupees early next week unless something further is done. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 close of interbank trading, the dollar was quoted at 36.77 rupees, up from 36.61 rupees late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1121GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds220116o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\