\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Seen Weak Amid Doubts On RBI Moves:Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By JYOTI PANDE \par \uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 1996\par 14:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-DJ)--Heavy dollar demand by importers and growing doubts over the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) commitment to protect the Indian rupee at a key level could push the Indian rupee to new lows in coming days, several analysts and traders say. \par \par \uc2  Despite continuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupee has been sliding lower, as demand for dollars steadily outpaces supply in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly sold dollars for rupees in India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday, in an effort to keep the dollar from rising uncontrollably against the rupee. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose sharply from 36.12 rupees at opening Wednesday to a high of 36.68 rupees in mid-afternoon trading, before significant dollar sales by the RBI pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to around 36.45 rupees around 1130 GMT. Compared to this, the dollar was below 35.00 rupees a little over a month ago, more specifically 34.98 rupees on the last trading day before Christmas. \par \par \uc2  Traders say that a normal upsurge in demand for dollars at the end of the month was exacerbated this time by some panic buying of dollars by importers, pushing the dollar sharply higher and causing further panic. \par \par \uc2  Much depends on the RBI's actions over the next few days, and dealers say that talking up the rupee would not succeed this time without some serious action by the government and the RBI. \par \par \uc2  Traders seemed to be waiting for some word from the finance ministry or the RBI which would indicate the RBI's commitment to protect the rupee against the dollar at a particular level. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 31-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1356GMT \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1v00vs6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
