\par\par \b \uc2  India's RBI Selling Dlrs -2: Dlr Rises Despite RBI Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1996\par 09:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-DJ)--The Reserve Bank of India sold U.S. dollars for rupees again Monday, at around 35.97 rupees in midday trading, continuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The demand for dollars continued to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, and traders said that the RBI was selling dollars in larger lots of around $5 million in an apparent effort to protect the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling below a particular level. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar sales by the RBI did not push the dollar down significantly, and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading around 35.97 rupees at 0730 GMT. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar is expected to rise further...it'll cross 36.00' rupees, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a European bank said, noting that the RBI has not been very successful in protecting the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vis a vis the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost credibility because it has not been able to keep the dollar from breaching' key psychological levels, he added. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-01-96 \par \par \uc2  0802GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1t00t89\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
