\par\par \b \uc2  Indian Rupee Weakens On Dlr Demand, Seen Lower Next Week \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1996\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-DJ)--The Indian rupee weakened Wednesday as the demand for dollars outpaced supply in moderate trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 35.82 rupees for most of the afternoon after opening a little lower at 35.81 rupees. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar is bid slightly today (Wednesday),' a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a foreign bank said, noting that a major state bank was buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Tuesday's limited demand due to a holiday in Calcutta, where its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are located. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 35.83 rupees around 1150 GMT, Wednesday, up from 35.765 rupees Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders did not expect much action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this week and expected weaker demand for the dollar, as Calcutta will also be closed for a holiday on Thursday and all banks nationwide will be closed Friday. \par \par \uc2  'There may be some action next week,' a dealer with a British bank said, noting that he expects month-end demand for dollars to boost the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and require \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't active in the market Wednesday, it has recently been selling dollars to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below around 35.90 rupees. But the trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't sustainable over a long period, and said the dollar could push through that point next week. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1210GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1o00qm2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
