\par\par \b \uc2  Indian Rupee Still Seen Weak Despite RBI Moves: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By TIMOTHY MAPES \par \uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1996\par 14:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-DJ)--Despite continuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI), many traders and analysts say heavy dollar demand from importers could push the Indian rupee to new lows in coming days. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank repeatedly sold dollars and bought rupees in India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday, the seventh-straight trading day in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped in to bolster the beleaguered rupee. \par \par \uc2  But while traders say the dollar sales have grown in strength in the past three days - indicating a growing concern on the part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the rupee - they add that the sales have only managed to stall the rupee's recent slide, not reverse it. \par \par \uc2  And although dealers say much depends on the RBI's actions over the next few days, they warn that unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains strength soon the rupee will soon fall below the all-time low of 35.90 rupees to the dollar, and could continue to spiral downward. \par \par \uc2  'The trend is still to march toward further depreciation,' says Lester Pereira, chief dealer at Barclays Bank in Bombay, who notes that demand for dollars remains strong, amid scanty supplies. \par \par \uc2  'The rupee could be around 37.00 (rupees to the dollar) levels by March,' adds Ravi Pai, chief dealer at HDFC Bank in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  In mid-afternoon trading Wednesday, the dollar was trading at 35.78 rupees, down slightly from 35.85 rupees late Tuesday but up nearly 2% from the start of January. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1324GMT \par \par \uc2  1139 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1a009c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
