\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee gains on Reserve Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Jan 10 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee gained marginally in late morning trade on Wednesday after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to suppress its fall, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said RBI sold dollars at 35.82 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The rupee gained to 35.74/77 per dollar from 35.84 opening. \par \par \uc2  Later, an RBI spokeswoman confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  without giving any details. \par \par \uc2  The rupee, which breached the 35 per dollar mark in recent weak, has been under pressure because of increased demand from Indian importers and a reluctance on the part of exporters to sell dollars on expectations of a further fall in the rupee. \par \par \uc2  A dealer said the RBI was more aggressive in the forward market on Tuesday, pushing down the six-month forward premium to 13.10 percent from around 16 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's forward market is yet to open. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers predicted further pressure on the rupee later in the day. "Banks are going to take advantage and stay long on dollars," said a dealer, referring to RBI's relaxation of overnight exposure limits last week. \par \par \uc2  -- Shyam Kumar +91-22-285 2851 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds1a09ftg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
