\par\par \b \uc2  Indian Rupee Weakens Slightly Despite RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1995\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-DJ)--The Indian rupee weakened slightly Tuesday despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the day, and traders said premiums for forward dollars rose in volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, money market rates also closed higher Tuesday, and money dealers said that the market looks ready to go up again Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Vigorous month-end demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to bolster the dollar, despite strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers predicted that the rupee would bounce back later in the week as dollars from foreign telecom companies that must pay license fees to the government begin to flow in. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 34.93 rupees at 1140 GMT, up from 34.92 rupees at late trading Monday, but down from Tuesday morning's rate of 34.96 rupees, where the RBI first sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  'The RBI spread the market liberally with dollars,' Tuesday, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a European bank said. He noted, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought the dollar down only for a short while, as there was enough corporate demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rebound within the hour. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums on six-month dollars rose to 2.73 rupees around 1140 GMT, up from 2.55 rupees at the opening and higher than 2.50 rupees-2.60 rupees Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1210GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbs09dmc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
