\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's RBI says  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Oct 30 (Reuter) - The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) interevened in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to arrest a fall in the value of the rupee against the dollar, an RBI official said. \par \par \uc2  The official declined to give details of the quantity of dollars sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened at 35.30/40 against the dollar and recovered to the 34.60/80 level on a statement by the Indian commerce minister that the rupee will not be allowed to fall further.  "They (RBI) sold (dollars) at 35.0 (rupees)," said a Bombay dealer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after demand for dollars threatened to push the rupee above 35.0 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," an RBI official told Reuters. She declined to say how much RBI sold and at what rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 34.88/98 in latest deals. \par \par \uc2  "RBI also sought forward quotes," said another bank dealer. The annualised premium fell to around 11 percent from 13.40 percent on the weekend, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said most of the business on Monday was in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  -- SHYAM KUMAR +91-22-285 2851 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drau02gmr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
