\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's RBI Gov/Rupee -4: Repeats Will Continue  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1995\par 11:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The RBI Governor's statement echoed comments made Sunday by Commerce Minister P. Chidambaram - who also referred to a recent drop in the rupee as an 'over-correction' - indicating that key Indian monetary officials are united in their resolve to defend the rupee. \par \par \uc2  The RBI also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in local markets Monday, pushing the rupee below 35.00 rupees, and the RBI Governor reiterated in his statement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to do so as needed. \par \par \uc2  'RBI will stand ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the objective of moderating the volatility in the exchange market while being consistent with the fundamentals,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Rangarajan added that expectations have played a part in the rupee's recent weakness. While importers left many of their positions uncovered during the two-years of stability, now that the rupee has fallen they have rushed to the market to cover. \par \par \uc2  Exporters, meanwhile, have responded by delaying the repatriation of their overseas earnings, Rangarajan noted. \par \par \uc2  'All these can result in a short-term dis-equilibrium between the supply and demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , thus exerting a pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It appears such a phenomenon has been in \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the recent period and it must get reversed,' Rangarajan said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1020G