\par\par \b \uc2  India: Bombay Shares Close Lower On Rupee Worries \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 1995\par 13:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-DJ)--Shares on the National Stock Exchange (NSE), the smaller bourse in Bombay, closed lower Tuesday as the falling value of the rupee vis-a-vis the dollar depressed sentiment, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) is closed Tuesday and Wednesday on account of a Hindu festival. \par \par \uc2  The rupee, which had fallen to a low of 35.85 rupees against the dollar Friday, remained under pressure hovering around 35.55 for the better part of the day. With \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants describing the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as half-hearted, dealers didn't rule out a further fall in the value of the rupee. \par \par \uc2  The precarious position of the rupee is sending shock waves through the NSE, said a dealer from Classic Share & Stockbroking Services Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds reason that they could sell their holdings and pick them back up when the rupee dwindles further. New foreign funds on the verge of entering the Indian market, may find it more attractive, but they too are watching to see where the rupee finally plateaus, said Nandkishore Gupta, chief executive of Indsec Share & Stockbroking Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Since several financial institutions, brokerages and the BSE weren't working Tuesday, volume on the NSE was thin. \par \par \uc2  'Usually institutions are around to buy when prices fall; today (Tuesday) they aren't working,' said the Classic dealer. \par \par \uc2  Shares of Reliance Industries Ltd. fell over 5 rupees and are expected to close at 250.50, against Monday's close of 255.75 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Shares of Tata Iron & Steel Co. fell 6 rupees and are expected to close at 241 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Gupta said trading on the NSE at a time when most of the other exchanges and institutions are closed has magnified the 'crisis-sentiment' in the equities markets, as dealers test the market with 'irresponsible' prices. The low prices on the terminals further depresses sentiment. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1116GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drao087a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
