\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee range-bound on RBI  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear. \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Oct 18 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee traded in a narrow band between 34.80-34.97 per dollar on Wednesday in a market where players were looking over their shoulders to see if the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Throughout the morning, the market was worried that RBI would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the 34.90 rupee level," a dealer said. As a result, many sold at 34.80 level for fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It (34.90) became a psychological barrier," said a dealer. The recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest the Indian rupee's slide was to bring stability to the market, said Shankar Acharya, a senior finance ministry official in New Delhi. \par \par \uc2  But a few bankers said they knew RBI would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 34.90, the level at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. "The rates were not that volatile today," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  "On Monday, the rupee fell by almost one rupee without large volumes being traded," said another dealer. "Today the movement was slow, and the market demand is more than what RBI can sell." \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a state-run bank said the highest level at which the dollar was sold was 34.96 and the lowest was 34.75. \par \par \uc2  "If the same trend continues, the dollar could touch the 36.0 rupee level by December," said Dayanand Nayak, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Corporation Bank. \par \par \uc2  A treasury manager with a city company said capital goods imports by many corporates had to be paid up before December end, the financial year closing of most international firms. \par \par \uc2  A leading Indian oil firm was also in the market for dollars to pay for large petroleum imports, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "RBI can't sell heavily to prop up the rupee without affecting its reserves," he said. \par \par \uc2  -- SHYAM KUMAR +91-22-285 2851 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drai02t77\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
