\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's RBI may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to support rupee - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 14 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee could get some support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossed the psychological barrier of 33 per dollar in early trade. \par \par \uc2  "Under the Reserve Bank of India's laws, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is supposed to either change its buying and selling rate for the dollar or keep the rupee within a five percent band of these rates," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI is very likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has fallen by around 5.0 percent from the RBI's buying rate of 31.37 per dollar after it hit the 33 level. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its buying and selling rates unchanged at 31.37 and 31.53 respectively. \par \par \uc2  RBI officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was trading at 33.10/15 per dollar in early trade after opening nearly unchanged at 32.83/86. \par \par \uc2  The dealers said the rupee may have found a new support at 33 rupees per dollar but no one was sure where the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stabilise. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has been falling against the dollar over the past fortnight mainly on dollar buying by state-run banks for the Indian government's foreign debt payments. \par \par \uc2  But with every fall many banks were reported to have taken speculative positions also, pushing the rupee down further. \par \par \uc2  "The initial nudge came from large demand for dollars from oil firms but the dollar buying for debt payments seem to have taken the bottom off," a dealer with a state-run bank said. \par \par \uc2  -- SUMIT SHARMA +91-22-285 2851 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9e0424s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
