\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Indian newspapers - Sept 6. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Prepared by New Delhi-based Business News and Information Services Pvt Ltd. for Reuters. Telephone no. 11-332-4842, fax 11-335-1006. Internet: Biznis.news@forums.sprintrpg.sprint.com) \par \par \uc2  TOP STORIES \par \par \uc2  The Hindustan Times \par \par \uc2  BEANT SINGH'S ASSASSIN IDENTIFIED; TWO ARRESTED \par \par \uc2  Police say they have unearthed a deadly plot behind the assassination of Punjab Chief Minister Beant Singh. Two people -- an engineer of a private firm, who designed the human bomb, and a Punjab police constable -- have been arrested in this connection. The identity of the person who is believed to have been used as the human bomb has also been established. \par \par \uc2  ----- \par \par \uc2  Indian Express \par \par \uc2  INDIA DENOUNCES PAKISTAN FOR POLITICISING WOMEN'S MEET \par \par \uc2  India has sharply denounced Pakistan for raising the Kashmir issue at the world women's conference at Beijing. India's Human Resources Development Minister Madhavrao Scindia told the second day's session of the conference in Beijing that Pakistan, instead of condemning and evolving measures to eliminate terrorism, had chosen to politicise issues by raising Kashmir. \par \par \uc2  ----- \par \par \uc2  VIOLENCE MARS AGRA STRIKE \par \par \uc2  N.D.Tiwari, the head of a rebel faction of India's ruling Congress party, was injured and arrested in Agra while leading a group of demonstrators in violation of prohibitory orders towards the Taj Mahal. The demonstrators were protesting against moves to relocate industries situated near the Taj Mahal. \par \par \uc2  ----- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab  TOP BUSINESS STORIES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Economic Times\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHANGES HINTED AT IN POWER POLICY TO ELIMINATE GREY AREAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government plans major changes in its power policy, including the abolition of two-part tariffs, removal of assured returns on equity and minimum plant-load factors, a fixed time frame for project execution, foreign equity returns and protection of foreign debt servicing from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuations and mandatory fuel-based bidding. Union Power Minister N.K.P. Salve said the ministry would soon constitute an expert committee to help frame the amended power policy. Competitive bidding on projects with fixed single tariff as the only criteria will remove all possibilities of capital cost padding, he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEW CENTRAL DEPOSITORY NORM GETS GOVERNMENT APPROVAL\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The cabinet has decided to bring forward legislation to set up a central depository in securities. The depository will provide computerised book-entry of securities, enabling transfer of ownership based on delivery of securities against payment of cash in listed or to-be-listed companies. The service will also provide computerised book entry of pledges of securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ENRON WILLING TO REDUCE TARIFF BY 10 PAISE PER UNIT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Dabhol Power Co (DPC) is willing to reduce the tariff for the first-phase of its $920 million project to 2.30 rupees per unit from 2.40 rupees proposed in the power purchase agreement. A company source said by effecting a change in fuel, the tariff for the first phase could be leveled at 10 paise less, besides ruling out any escalation. DPC is also willing to give up the fuel management contract to Maharashtra State Electricity Board and induct an Indian partner with 30 percent equity stake.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RESERVE BANK TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF RUPEE SLIDE CONTINUES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI) is closely monitoring the slide of the rupee against the dollar as it touched this year's lowest, but there are no clear indications yet as to the level at which it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The spot dollar opened at 31.88-31.90 rupee levels on Tuesday and crossed the immediate pre-budget low of Rs 32.15 to touch Rs 32.57. RBI officials said the RBI had not resorted to any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the current fluctuation in the rupee was purely on account of demand and supply factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONDA MOTOR TO PICK UP 51 PCT STAKE IN CAR VENTURE WITH SIEL\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Honda Motor Co will pick up 51 percent equity in its proposed car joint venture with the Siddharth Sriram group's flagship, SIEL Ltd. SIEL, like DCM in its joint venture with Daewoo, will hold a minority stake in the proposed joint venture. According to sources, the Honda-SIEL car is expected to hit the road late in 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RESERVE BANK SEEKS HIKE IN FOREIGN EQUITY LEVEL\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Reserve Bank of India has approached the Finance Ministry to raise the foreign equity participation level from the present 51 percent to 74 percent in the case of joint ventures with foreign financial participation for automatic approval. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has taken up the issue of increasing the scope for automatic approval of foreign financial collaborations and raising statutory foreign investment limits with the government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Business Standard\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOURSE TIGHTENS MARGINS TO CURB PRICE RIGGING IN CASH GROUP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) has tightened its margin system for non-specified (cash) shares to clamp down on overtrading in B-group shares. The system comes into effect from the new settlement period starting Monday. The BSE has replaced the flat margin of 20 percent on scrip-wise net positions by a graded but tough set of margins.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDIA'S RELIANCE SETS SIGHTS ON U.S. OIL EXPLORATION COMPANY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reliance Industries Ltd is examining the possibility of taking over a U.S. oil exploration company Santa Fe Energy. Sources said Reliance has held talks with the Houston-based company for a possible takeover. The acquisition will serve Reliance's purpose of arranging a long-term crude oil source for the 15 million tonne refinery it is setting up in India's Gujarat state.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORD, MAHINDRAS SEEK APPROVAL FOR $800 MLN VENTURE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ford Motor Co of the U.S. and India's Mahindra & Mahindra have filed an application with Foreign Investment Promotion Board (FIPB) for approval to establish a joint venture company to manufacture Ford vehicles. The proposal envisages an investment of more than $800 million in the venture in which the two partners will hold 50 percent stakes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Financial Express\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOMBAY BOURSE TO SUSPEND TRADING IN 1,000 SCRIPS NEXT WEEK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bombay bourse has decided to suspend trading in nearly 1,000 companies from Monday till further notice. According to top bourse officials, these companies have failed to adhere to clause 16 of the listing agreement of the exchange which stipulates that adequate notice of book closure/record date be mentioned.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Observer of Business and Politics\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ELECTRICITY BOARD EASES NORMS FOR PRIVATE PROJECT CLEARANCE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Central Electricity Authority (CEA) has streamlined its norms for faster clearance of private power projects following criticism for slow appraisal of projects. Clearance for a project may now be granted within a month of an application being filed. The techno-economic clearance would take about two months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FIRE TEST MUST FOR RAYONS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A flammability test certificate will be mandatory for all rayon chiffon garments exported from India including skirts, blouses, dresses and scarves. Textile Secretary T.S.R. Subramaniam said the rule was extended to scarves as the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission recently confirmed that 100 percent chiffon scarves had not met the U.S. government's flamability standards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DELHI BOURSE TO BRING ALL NORTHERN BOURSES UNDER ONE UMBRELLA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Delhi bourse plans to bring all bourses in the northern region under one umbrella in an attempt to boost liquidity and business of its member-brokers. According to the plan, Delhi bourse members would be allowed to give terminals to their counterparts of other stock exchanges, who will deal on sub-terminals of original members.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1995\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9604a4u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
